		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Looking Forward]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2174&amp;p=18053#p18053"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br><br>Just back from a week trip and used the MD-9600 as my mobile and a base station in the BnB I stayed. Not a single issue for me, worked great. So a great big thank you to all.<br><br>Through my local radio club I have access to a full test bench and equipment and am able to accurately measure RF power, Frequency, and track any drift. As such I am arranging to have the time to calibrate all my HT's and this got me thinking about the MD9600. I am aware that currently you do not have access to calibrate the MD-9600 with the Open CPS like you do with the GD77. I am curious if at some time in the future the CPS will be able to allow calibration of the MD-9600 radio?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1814">AA3RP</a> — Mon Mar 28, 2022 4:31 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
